Subject: [PATCH 09805/11362] [outer-loop] Disposition exp3403: a claim refuted
 by its own data

CLAIM_REFUTED_BY_OWN_DATA on experiment_3403_archive_v313_activate_v314.
ACCEPTED. Verified against the artifact, not taken from the report: it
declares honest_verdict "complete: archive_v313_activate_v314_ready=true"
and archive_v313_activate_v314_ready: True, while carrying
blocked_artifacts: ["exp3392-gatemate-n16-bootstrap-fix"] in the same
file. The claim of complete archival is refuted by the artifact's own
inventory.

This is a different and stronger class than the five rows above it.
exp6478 and exp6497 were circular-oracle; exp6544 and exp6546 were
strawman-baseline. All four needed a judgement about whether the
evidence supported the claim. This one needs no judgement at all: the
artifact contains both the assertion and its counterexample.

That difference matters for prevention. Each earlier row ended with "no
lint detects this shape", because deciding whether a baseline was a real
threat, or whether a verifier was the oracle, is exactly the reasoning
the claim audit exists to do. A terminal complete:/success: verdict
alongside a non-empty blocked_* list has no legitimate reading, so a
mechanical check has no false-positive surface to worry about. It is the
first finding in this ledger that converts cleanly into a check, and it
should be built before the next archive task repeats it.

Consequence for the record: the v313 archive is not evidence that v313
closed cleanly, and any chain treating v314 activation as gated on a
complete v313 inherits a false premise. What was archived still stands;
the readiness flag does not.

Artifact left unedited per never-prune.

